    "notes": [
      "One inductor does both directions: charging steps 5 V on VIN down to the battery, discharging steps the battery up to 5.1 V on VOUT; VIN passes to VOUT while charging.",
      "The datasheet's figure adds a flashlight LED from KEY through 20 ohm, and USB data-line dividers (43k/75k, 51k/51k) so phones draw full current; leave out what you do not need.",
      "Heat leaves through the exposed pad: a GND pour with vias under it; keep SW - L1 - C2 and VOUT - C3 loops short.",
      "Not placed by the support circuit, add it where the board needs it: D1_D4 4 LEDs between LED1, LED2, LED3 (25/50/75/100 % gauge: D1 and D2 antiparallel between LED1 and LED2, D3 and D4 antiparallel between LED2 and LED3 (Figure 7))."
    ],
    "page": "p. 9, Figure 7 (4 LEDs SOC indicator typical application schematic)"
